---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | konh" description="About this publishing setup.">
  <section class="container article">
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="meta-line">About this stack</span>
      <h1>Git first, editor flexible.</h1>
      <p>
        This site keeps the canonical copy in Markdown and MDX. Obsidian, Cursor, VS Code, or a Git-based CMS can all
        edit the same source without trapping the archive in a platform.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="article-body">
      <h2>Default workflow</h2>
      <p>Write in <code>src/content/posts</code>, keep images in <code>public/images</code>, then push to GitHub.</p>
      <h2>Optional CMS</h2>
      <p>
        The <code>public/admin</code> directory includes a Sveltia CMS entrypoint. Connect it to a GitHub repo when you
        want browser-based editing.
      </p>
      <h2>Optional Notion bridge</h2>
      <p>
        Notion can remain a draft inbox, but published content should be exported into this repo so the live site has no
        runtime dependency on Notion.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="toc">
      <strong>Stack</strong>
      Astro 6<br />
      MDX<br />
      Pagefind<br />
      RSS<br />
      Sveltia CMS-ready
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
